  "createdAt" : 1680793834,
  "description" : "This dataset contains undergraduate tuition and mandatory fees for each public Massachusetts institution of higher education since fiscal year 2006 (FY06). Data are disaggregated by fiscal year, segment, institution, and student residency.\n\nThese annual rates are based on full-time, undergraduate, state-supported tuition and mandatory fees, as published in the fall.\n\nThis dataset contains two versions of tuition and mandatory fee data:\n<b>1) Nominal/Published Rates:</b> the published tuition and fees for a given year, reflecting the actual cost at the time.\n<b>2) Inflation-Adjusted Rates:</b> tuition and fees adjusted for inflation using 2024 dollars, to provide a consistent comparison of the cost of college over time.\n\nThis dataset is 1 of 2 underlying datasets used in the interactive\n<a href=\"https://www.mass.edu/datacenter/factbook/tuitionfees.asp\">Tuition and Fees dashboard</a> on the Department of Higher Education Data Center:\n\n1) <a href=\"https://educationtocareer.data.mass.gov/College-and-Career/Public-Postsecondary-Tuition-and-Fees/3bpk-k8k2/about_data\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> Public Postsecondary Tuition and Fees</a>\n2) <a href=\"https://educationtocareer.data.mass.gov/dataset/Public-Postsecondary-Weighted-Tuition-and-Fees-by-/phn7-2pa8/about_data\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> Weighted Average Tuition and Fees by Public Postsecondary Segment</a>\n\nNotes:\n- Data appear as reported to the Massachusetts Department of Higher Education.\n- Figures published by DHE may differ slightly from figures published by other institutions and organizations due to differences in timing of publication, data definitions, and calculation logic.\n- A fiscal year (FY) is 12-month period beginning July 1 and ending June 30. Because a fiscal year straddles two different calendar years, the calendar year and fiscal year will not always match. For example, FY 2025 runs from July 1, 2024 to June 30, 2025.\n- Columns ADJ_TUITION_2024, ADJ_MAND_FEES_2024, and ADJ_TUITION_AND_MAND_FEES_2024 are adjusted for inflation using the <a href=\"https://www.bls.gov/cpi/tables/supplemental-files/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers (CPI-U)</a> from the Bureau of Labor Statistics. Rates are converted to 2024 dollars to allow for consistence comparisons over time.",
